@ [portion_slice_map] docs/planning/Portion_And_Slice_Map.v1.sop

& [CanonicalRecord: WholePieWorkingPattern] is the processed planning authority for LangSOP whole-pie development
  + [canonical_uuid] is ecc5770f-e6a6-40cc-b5a2-b07e5853c69b
  + [source_manifest_uuid] is d5a78c55-233b-4b03-b3ce-a79ef26067bd
  + [exploded_uuid] is 3f620214-4da2-4d8a-96f2-74ee82097ba2
  + [product_uuid] is ee4fda0b-8433-4301-8c6f-648da69f4b7f
  + [portion_slice_map_uuid] is 7f03db1d-3818-4acd-a42f-a306e26e4a39
  + [authority_scope] is product overview, portion model, slice-family model, slice lifecycle, rebake cycle, surface implications, and model-routing pattern
  + [implementation_scope] is planning and decomposition authority only
  + [depends_on] is docs/canonical/LangSOP_Initial_Workflow.v2.canonical.sop

  = must: use whole-pie development as the default LangSOP planning pattern
  = must: keep product overview and portion map loaded before slice minting
  = must: treat slices as generated derived work packets, not source truth
  = must: require completion review before newly completed work influences the next slice
  = must: preserve blocked portions inside the whole product map
  - never: create implementation slices from blocked portions except blocker-resolution or preparation slices

& [CanonicalWholePieProductContract] is the product-level planning contract
  + [whole_product] is LangSOP Manager Layer
  + [product_job] is preserve authority, narrative, coordination, readiness, packetization, proof, and reentry across multi-user and multi-agent work
  + [source_of_truth] is SOP source, signed canonical artifacts, proof-backed kernel records, and explicit human overrides
  + [projection_set] is manager, worker, narrative, debug, chat, Codex, terminal, IRC, Matrix, web, and optional Langflow surfaces

  = must: expose whole-product state before local slice execution
  = must: keep surfaces as projections with visible authority and freshness notices
  = must: keep LangGraph as procedure over kernel records, not source authority

& [CanonicalPortionContract] is the product portion contract
  + [portion] is a large product territory with stable purpose, boundary, requirements, dependencies, support gaps, proof route, surface implications, and slice families
  + [portion_state_set] is desired, specified, supported, blocked, deferred, ready_for_slice_family, active, verified, stale, and superseded
  + [portion_record_contract] is PortionRecordContract from the exploded specification

  = must: define and review portions before slice families are minted
  = must: keep dependencies and support gaps explicit
  = must: allow a portion to remain baked into the whole while unsliced
  = must: rebake portion state when completed work changes support or requirements

& [CanonicalSliceContract] is the work-slice contract
  + [slice_family] is the reusable subdivision of a portion around coherent work
  + [slice] is a generated work packet with authority basis, preconditions, expected outputs, verification oracle, model route, and completion-review requirement
  + [task] is an execution detail inside a slice
  + [slice_state_set] is candidate, blocked, ready, assigned, in_progress, completed, verified, stale, superseded, and invalidated

  = must: mint slices from current readiness projections
  = must: mark stale slices stale when source, support, dependency, proof, or freshness changes
  = must: attach verification_oracle and model_route to every slice
  = must: classify each slice as GPT-5.3-Codex-Spark-suitable or requires deeper reasoning
  - never: let task lists carry authority that belongs on the slice record

& [CanonicalRebakeCycle] is the repeatable development loop
  + [step_1] is load product overview, portion map, and current capability field
  + [step_2] is choose portion or support gap by frontier order, risk, readiness, and user priority
  + [step_3] is recompute readiness from support, dependencies, proof, freshness, ownership, and coordination
  + [step_4] is mint slices with authority basis, forbidden scope, expected outputs, and verification oracle
  + [step_5] is execute slice and capture proof, notes, faults, and changed artifacts
  + [step_6] is review completed work for support_delta and requirement_delta
  + [step_7] is update product overview, portion map, capability field, and stale slice markers
  + [step_8] is mint the next clean slice or rebake the whole when learning changes product shape

  = must: apply this cycle whenever LangSOP work decomposes from product intent into executable work
  = must: treat rebake as expected learning, not planning failure
  = must: update or supersede stale slices rather than carrying them forward silently

& [CanonicalModelRoutingPattern] is the model-routing authority for the working pattern
  + [requires_deeper_reasoning] is whole-product rebake, portion boundary changes, schema and natural-key design, authority semantics, storage decision, ambiguous fault handling, and operations safety
  + [GPT-5.3-Codex-Spark-suitable] is bounded implementation, fixtures, tests, lint fixes, ledger updates, projection rendering, and proof updates after contracts stabilize

  = must: state whether each proposed slice is GPT-5.3-Codex-Spark-suitable or requires deeper reasoning
  = must: reserve deeper reasoning for architecture, ambiguous debugging, cross-system integration, unstable specifications, and high-risk design choices

